CRITICAL SAFETY WARNING — PLEASE READ BEFORE USE

This skill gives an AI agent (Claude or any skill-aware assistant) the
ability to read, write, and delete files in your karpathy-wiki repo on
the local filesystem. It writes new wiki pages, modifies existing
pages (frontmatter and body), deletes pages during unwind operations,
appends to wiki/log.md, and commits + pushes to the repo's git remote.
Operations run with full read/write privileges. There is NO sandboxing
and NO per-call confirmation — the only safeguards are instructions in
the skill telling the agent to surface destructive changes before
performing them and to operate only from inside the wiki repo's root.

Potential consequences of misuse include but are not limited to:
- Permanent deletion of wiki pages (after git push)
- Overwriting page contents during ingest or refresh
- Mass-rewriting of cross-references during unwind
- Silent or bulk modification of frontmatter, sections, or links
- Mistaken push of wiki changes to a public remote
- Acting on prompt injection embedded in raw/ source material

Risks specific to AI-driven use:
- An agent may misinterpret a request and run a destructive operation
- A prompt-injection payload reaching the agent (via web articles,
  papers, transcripts, or pasted material in raw/) could direct it to
  overwrite, delete, or rewrite unrelated pages, or to push commits
- A hallucinated source slug may produce unintended writes
- A buggy script update could mass-rewrite links incorrectly

Recovery expectations:
- The wiki repo is git-tracked; `git reflog` and the remote serve as
  the primary recovery backstops. After a git push, recovery depends
  on remote retention policies.
- The skill itself maintains no backups outside git.

